{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n`rebar review-code` runs the same four-pass reviewer the Gerrit bot casts `LLM-Review`\nwith, so an author can preview code-review findings locally before pushing — the exact\nanalog of `rebar review-plan` for the plan gate. But the code-review on-ramp never\nmentions it: the plan-review author can discover their local self-check, the code-review\nauthor cannot. This closes that discoverability asymmetry so both gates read symmetrically.\n\n## Approach\nSurface `rebar review-code` in the same three places plan review's local self-check is\nsurfaced: the author on-ramp (`src/rebar/_guides/passing-code-review.md`, printed by `rebar explain\nreview`), the docs index (`docs/README.md`), and the canonical `AGENTS.md` pointer.\nRejected: adding a new `rebar explain` topic for local code review — the existing `review`\nguide is the right home, and a second topic would fragment the on-ramp rather than fix\ndiscoverability.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/_guides/passing-code-review.md  (new \"Preview the review locally\" section, intro cross-link, loop-diagram preview step)\n- docs/README.md               (index entry mentions the local preview)\n- AGENTS.md                    (code-review pointer names `rebar review-code`)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `src/rebar/_guides/passing-code-review.md` has a \"Preview the review locally\" section teaching\n      `rebar review-code`, incl. the `[agents]` extra and `REBAR_VERIFY_ENABLE_CODE_REVIEW`\n      enabling requirement; verified by\n      `grep -q 'REBAR_VERIFY_ENABLE_CODE_REVIEW' src/rebar/_guides/passing-code-review.md && grep -q '## Preview the review locally' src/rebar/_guides/passing-code-review.md`.\n- [ ] The loop diagram in `src/rebar/_guides/passing-code-review.md` shows the optional local\n      `rebar review-code` preview step; verified by\n      `grep -q 'rebar review-code — optional local preview' src/rebar/_guides/passing-code-review.md`.\n- [ ] The `docs/README.md` passing-code-review index entry names `rebar review-code`;\n      verified by `grep -A2 'passing-code-review.md)\\*\\*' docs/README.md | grep -q 'rebar review-code'`.\n- [ ] `AGENTS.md` code-review pointer names `rebar review-code`; verified by\n      `grep -q 'preview the review locally with .rebar review-code' AGENTS.md`.\n- [ ] The intro anchor link resolves to the new section heading (GitHub-generated anchor\n      `#preview-the-review-locally-before-you-push` matches the heading text); verified by\n      `grep -q '#preview-the-review-locally-before-you-push' src/rebar/_guides/passing-code-review.md`.\n\n## Criteria correction (2026-07-24)\nThe criteria above originally named `docs/passing-code-review.md`. Commit c2bfbe217\n(\"package author guides in-package so `rebar explain` works from any directory\") later moved\nthe guide to `src/rebar/_guides/passing-code-review.md` and left the old path a pointer stub,\nwhich made every grep in this ticket false even though the work was delivered and is intact at\nthe new path.\n\nThis ticket was first closed with `--ref f90850861` (the commit the work landed in). That\nverified, but it left the criteria asserting checks that no longer hold — inaccurate state in\nthe shared ticket store. Per the remedy now documented in `docs/plan-review-gate.md`\n(\"When the acceptance criteria no longer match reality\", ticket 4636-432a-1871-4d74), the\ncriteria have been corrected to name the guide's real location and the ticket re-closed against\nthem. The delivered content is unchanged; only the paths in the criteria moved.\n"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1784949273364374001,"uuid":"b13f29b5-61bc-4674-a35b-eba6bc55b8d1"}